Package: xorg-server-legacy-nvidia-19
Architecture: amd64 i386
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, nvidia-legacy-xserver-common
Recommends: nvidia-legacy-173xx-driver
Description: private Xorg 1.15.1 (video ABI 19) for legacy NVIDIA blobs
 A co-installable build of xorg-server 1.15.1, installed under
 /opt/nvidia-legacy/xserver-19/ and launched only via the
 "Xorg (NVIDIA legacy)" login session. It provides X server video driver ABI
 19, which the NVIDIA 173xx nvidia_drv.so needs and which the
 distribution X server (a much newer ABI) does not offer.
 .
 The distribution's own Xorg, Wayland and all other sessions are untouched.
 .
 SECURITY: an old X server receives no upstream fixes and is a larger attack
 surface. Local-session CVEs are backported in debian/patches/1.15.1/security/.
 Use only where the hardware leaves no alternative; prefer an isolated machine.

Package: nvidia-legacy-xserver-common
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: launcher + session for the private legacy NVIDIA X servers
 The nvidia-legacy-xserver wrapper, the Xsession glue and the
 "Xorg (NVIDIA legacy)" desktop-session file shared by every
 xorg-server-legacy-nvidia-* package.
